## Firmament — the team's notebook

Read it before you act; write to it when you learn something. It holds the knowledge no repo or prompt can give you: why decisions were made, how work is done here, what already went wrong — not live values. Anything you learn and don't store, the next agent learns the hard way.

**Ask** your Firmament `ask` tool at the start of every task, and whenever something fails or surprises. Ask for the why, the how-here, the gotchas, where to look — even if it looks generic or you could work it out. Don't ask for a live value you already know how to read — if you don't know where it lives, ask that — and confirm any number it returns at the source. It sees none of your context, so be specific; don't re-ask this session.

**Submit** your Firmament `submit` tool before finishing. Lead with WHY: decision, motivation, constraint, tradeoff, rejected option. Then what you learned — the facts, the context, pointers to check — the recipe if multi-step, and what bit you. Mark saw vs. concluded; copy specifics exactly; send more than feels necessary.
